Data   : IncidentTimelinePageViewModel binds the shared S7 IncidentRepository (web useIncident GET /status/incidents/{id})
         via incidentTimelinePageSourceOf(); the two writes are the repository's non-throwing Result mutations —
         appendIncidentUpdate() (web useAppendIncidentUpdate POST …/updates) and patchIncident(resolved=true) (web
         usePatchIncident PATCH …). On a successful write the repository evicts the incident cache partition and the
         view-model refreshes the read, so the header + timeline reflect the change (web invalidate ['status-incidents']).
         No HTTP in the view. The host builds a page-local HttpIncidentRepository over container.api + container.cacheStore,
         exactly as the sibling CommandsRoute builds its own HttpCommandsRepository (the Android DI graph wires no
         IncidentsStore yet).
Adapt  : keep-previous-data (web React-Query parity) — a successful append/resolve evicts the cache, so the re-read
         briefly emits Loading(cached=null). mergeKeepingIncidentData (runningFold) carries the last-loaded incident into
         that slot so the timeline stays on screen (flagged refreshing) instead of flashing the first-load spinner;
         `isLoading` is true only on the genuine first load (web `if (isLoading)`). A missing/non-positive route id
         (web `Number.isFinite && > 0 ? … : null` → `error || !incident`) resolves straight to the not-found surface.
Strings: the web page predates i18n and hard-codes its English copy (no useTranslation), so the auto-generated
         translation_* catalog carries no key for it. A hand-authored res/values/incident_timeline_strings.xml supplies
         every literal (verbatim from the web source) so every visible string resolves via stringResource — the same
         *_strings.xml mechanism as incident_form_strings.xml / nav_strings.xml. The duration abbreviations (s/m/h/d) are
         language-neutral and reproduced verbatim from the web template literals (CommandsPage "15s" precedent), so they
         carry no key. The auto-generated strings.xml is NOT edited (no drift).
Nav    : Destinations 'incidentTimeline' -> /system-status/incidents/:id (arg id) pre-existing (Destinations.kt:160;
         count unchanged); host wired via PageHosts.register; Back -> /system-status opened through the app's own
         teslasync://app deep-link scheme (AndroidManifest + TeslaSyncNavHost) since no NavController is exposed to hosts.
Scope  : the web page also renders <AIIncidentTimelineSummarizer incidentId> — a SEPARATELY-ledgered shared surface
         (shared-surfaces/AIIncidentTimelineSummarizer) gated off by default whose Android source needs an AI-mode gate +
         SSE client the Android DI graph does not expose yet (its own comment: "streaming atoms are the out-of-scope P3
         component-library bundle"). It is NOT this unit's parity (PARITY_REQUIRED enumerates the 4 GlassPanels + 2
         states); the deterministic timeline this page renders IS the canonical surface (web comment §I3/§I5). Not embedded
         here by design, documented (Honesty Covenant #9), not silently dropped.

